# Savoy Capital — environment. Copy to `.env.local` for development and set the
# same variables on the Railway service for the deploy. Never commit real keys:
# `.gitignore` allows this example through and blocks every other `.env*`.

# ── Clerk ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# From the Clerk Dashboard → API keys, for the instance backing this
# environment. The publishable key is shipped to the browser (that is what
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ means and it is fine); the secret key must never be.
#
# Both are REQUIRED for the app to build and to boot. A deploy without them
# fails rather than serving the private surface unprotected.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
CLERK_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ── Who may open the portfolio monitor ─────────────────────────────────────
# Nothing to set. Access is whoever the principals invited: the Clerk instance
# is set to RESTRICTED sign-up, so an account cannot exist unless it was
# invited, and "signed in" therefore means "allowed in".
#
# The consequence, so it is not discovered late: if sign-up is ever set back to
# PUBLIC in the Clerk Dashboard, the portfolio monitor opens to anyone who
# signs up, and nothing in this repo will detect it. That setting is the
# boundary. See .claudet/PLAYBOOKS/auth-clerk.md GOTCHA 3.

# ── Cloudflare R2 — the document store ─────────────────────────────────────
# From the Cloudflare dashboard → R2 → Manage R2 API Tokens → Create API Token.
# Scope the token to THIS BUCKET ONLY, with "Object Read & Write" — never
# "Admin Read & Write", which can create and delete buckets the app never
# touches.
#
# NONE of these may take a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix. That prefix inlines a value
# into the browser bundle, which for the secret key would publish it to every
# visitor. The Clerk publishable key above carries the prefix legitimately;
# these do not.
#
# The S3 endpoint is DERIVED from the account id in src/lib/r2.ts, so there is
# deliberately no R2_ENDPOINT variable to disagree with it.
#
# OPTIONAL: the app builds and boots without them. The file routes answer 503
# when they are absent; every other page is unaffected.
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
R2_BUCKET=savoycapital
